  "changes": [
    "Providers and Firebase Admin services load on first use in the CommonJS build. Upstream's v1 and v2 indexes require every provider, and the providers require Firestore, Auth, App Check and the Realtime Database client, at import: importing firebase-functions/v2 for its logger loaded 663 modules. Firebase Admin services also load on first use in the ES module build.",
    "onInit callbacks run once for concurrent first invocations; a failed run is retried by the next invocation. Upstream ran the callback once per invocation that arrived before it finished.",
    "The firebase-functions bin reads its documented [functionsDir] argument. Upstream read it only when two or more arguments were given.",
    "Realtime Database snapshots read data as before; DataSnapshot#ref, which needs the Realtime Database client, throws vfirebase-admin's descriptive error.",
    "Public declarations need no ambient Node types and use vcors and vexpress declarations instead of @types/cors and @types/express.",
    "Structured logging preserves null-prototype query objects and shadowed property names, handles BigInt and cyclic toJSON results, bounds nesting, and does not mutate frozen entries when adding trace context.",
    "CommonJS and ESM logger, trace context and initialization share identity and state. A previous initializer finishing cannot mark a newer registration complete.",
    "Deployment serialization returns a new wire representation without modifying frozen or reusable endpoint declarations. An explicit worklist handles deeply nested declarations without recursive stack overflow.",
    "HTTP CORS completion removes its finish listener when either preflight or the handler finishes. HTTP/callable/scheduler factories, options and manifest helpers share CJS/ESM module identity.",
    "Callable payloads preserve own __proto__ keys, ignore inherited type markers and reject cycles deliberately. Deep payloads avoid unbounded recursion. Request data must be an own property.",
    "Callable status names cannot resolve through Object.prototype. Stream writes tolerate synchronous callbacks, pending writes resolve false on disconnect, and response listeners are removed at completion. CommonJS and ESM callable helpers share identity.",
    "Secret JSON parse errors no longer include the parser diagnostic, which can quote secret contents. CJS/ESM parameter identities and registration lists are shared; duplicate names are fully replaced.",
    "Firestore changed events decode protobuf once, static path patterns are compiled at definition time, and own prototype-named captures are preserved. Field-mask sibling changes accumulate safely. Timestamp conversion handles timezone offsets and pre-epoch nanoseconds."
  ],
  "implementation": {
    "kind": "upstream-fork-with-independent-components",
    "replacementStatus": "independent implementation pending",
    "targetScope": "HTTP and callable handlers, logger, secret parameters, schedules and Firestore triggers.",
    "independentComponents": {
      "lib/logger/index.js": "Own structured logging implementation with bounded, path-aware serialization, non-mutating trace enrichment and standard formatting. ESM forwards to the same implementation.",
      "lib/common/onInit.js": "Own registration state machine: concurrent calls share a pending run; failure retries, and each replacement registration owns its completion. ESM shares the same state.",
      "lib/runtime/manifest.js": "Independent table-driven reset defaults and iterative, non-mutating manifest serialization; frozen inputs and 15,000-level declarations are supported. ESM forwards to the same module.",
      "lib/v2/options.js": "Independent option projection tables, timeout validation and network configuration assembly, preserving the existing deployment protocol and shared global-options registry.",
      "lib/runtime/definition.js": "Own shared function-definition builder separates HTTP/callable/scheduler trigger metadata from invocation pipelines.",
      "lib/v2/providers/https.js": "Own HTTP/callable factories and CORS completion lifecycle, using the independent callable transport and shared function-definition builder.",
      "lib/v2/providers/scheduler.js": "Own schedule factory and invocation adapter; shares the deployment builder and CJS/ESM identity.",
      "lib/common/providers/https.js": "Source-informed independent request validation, emulator-context adapter, CORS lifecycle and invocation composition. Upstream protocol, diagnostics and tests informed the rewrite; this is not a clean-room claim. ESM forwards to this implementation.",
      "lib/runtime/callable-auth.js": "Own verification orchestration. Production tokens are still verified by the retained Admin SDK; authentication policy and App Check enforcement are preserved. Unsafe decoding remains restricted to the existing explicit debug feature.",
      "lib/runtime/callable-codec.js": "Own bounded-recursion traversal with a deep-data worklist, ancestor cycle detection and safe own-property copying. Firebase numeric wrapper conversion remains compatible.",
      "lib/runtime/callable-error.js": "Own error class using canonical Google RPC status data; rejects inherited property names and protects the shared status records.",
      "lib/runtime/callable-response.js": "Own request-scoped response lifecycle: cancellation, heartbeat scheduling, SSE output, pending-write cancellation and listener disposal. Handles synchronous write callbacks and rejects writes after completion.",
      "lib/params/index.js": "Own parameter registration facade, preserving shared array identities, declaration order and manifest projection while removing all duplicate names. CJS/ESM share identity. Generic expression classes still retain upstream implementations.",
      "lib/runtime/secret-parameter.js": "Own string and JSON secret accessors with runtime-only access guards, dynamic environment reads and JSON diagnostics that omit parser excerpts of secret contents.",
